  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enterprise Development Program - Honduras</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam&apos;s Enterprise Development Programme (EDP) invests in small and medium enterprises (SMEs) that have potential to create significant social impact but lack the capabilities and resources for growth. Enterprises are carefully screened and approved by an independent investment committee. They receive an intelligent mix of loans, grants, and business development services. They tend to be more marginalised, physically and economically, than the SMEs supported by banks and mainstream investors.  EDP works closely with local business development service providers, financial institutions,  governments, universities, Non Governmental Organisations (NGOs), and mentors. Through a portfolio of viable and growing enterprises EDP supports the creation of new jobs and sustainable income generating opportunities, focused on empowering women as suppliers, employees and decision makers. Evidence from the programme is used to influence local governments and donors as well as international impact investors. Programme aims to:  - Support the development of sustainable enterprises that would otherwise remain marginalised  - Secure and increase household incomes for vulnerable populations  - Increase women&apos;s participation and create opportunities for women&apos;s economic empowerment (WEE)  - Ensure all stakeholders get a fair share of the value generated by the enterprise  - Demonstrate SME investment approaches that can reach poorer excluded groups and empower women</narrative>
  </description>
